{
  "benchmark_id": 213,
  "prompt": "Write a function that takes two parameters: an array of instance objects (instances) and a target object (target). Each instance object has a 'path' property (string) and a 'sort' property (array). The function should modify the instances array: for the first instance (index 0), replace it entirely with the target object. For all other instances, replace the 'path' property by replacing the original first instance's path prefix with the target's path, and replace the 'sort' property by concatenating the target's sort array with the remaining elements from the original instance's sort array (after removing the prefix that matches the first instance's sort). The function should return the modified instances array.The output is the modified instances array.\n\n    Only return the code, don't include any other information,\n    such as a preamble or suffix.\n",
  "implementation_details": "Language: JavaScript. Iterate over the array to update path and sort fields and return the modified JSON object.",
  "fc_tests": [
    {
      "test_id": 0,
      "input": {
        "instances": [
          {
            "path": "/a",
            "sort": [
              "a"
            ]
          },
          {
            "path": "/a/c",
            "sort": [
              "a",
              "c"
            ]
          }
        ],
        "target": {
          "path": "/b",
          "sort": [
            "b"
          ]
        }
      },
      "expected_output": [
        {
          "path": "/b",
          "sort": [
            "b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "/b/c",
          "sort": [
            "b",
            "c"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
